  "question": "Let $\\vec{a} = 3\\hat{i} + \\lambda\\hat{j} - \\hat{k}$ and $\\vec{b} = \\hat{i} + \\hat{j} + 2\\hat{k}$. If the projection of $\\vec{a}$ on $\\vec{b}$ is $1$, find $\\lambda$.",
  "answeroption": "B",
  "explanation": "Projection of $\\vec{a}$ on $\\vec{b}$ is $\\frac{\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b}}{|\\vec{b}|}=1$<br /><br />Compute $\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b} = 3 \\times 1 + \\lambda \\times 1 + (-1) \\times 2 = 3 + \\lambda - 2 = \\lambda + 1$<br /><br />$|\\vec{b}| = \\sqrt{1^2 + 1^2 + 2^2} = \\sqrt{6}$<br /><br />So,<br /><br />$\\frac{\\lambda + 1}{\\sqrt{6}} = 1$<br /><br />$\\lambda + 1 = \\sqrt{6}$<br /><br />$\\lambda = \\sqrt{6} - 1$<br /><br />Hence, $\\boxed{\\lambda = \\sqrt{6}-1}$.",
  "explanation_image": [],
  "options": {
    "A": "$\\sqrt{6}+1$",
    "B": "$\\sqrt{6}-1$",
    "C": "$1-\\sqrt{6}$",
    "D": "$\\sqrt{3}-1$"
  },
